  "name": "Bodyweight Single-Leg Hip Thrust",
  "definition": "A one-leg bench-supported hip thrust from the Boxing Science exercise library. The upper back rests on a bench, one heel remains planted with toes lifted, and the opposite leg stays lifted with its knee near a right angle. Hip extension raises the pelvis to neutral. There is no external resistance or comparable load; the floor bridge and band-resisted thrust remain separate fixtures. Knee-extension and vasti roles are categorical transfers from the reviewed banded and barbell hip-thrust mechanics, not directly measured in this unweighted fixture.",
